                    {
                        "translation_id": "bd726ce7-63e6-4fcc-8360-7032b6c2f79d",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f02d9f4-9d49-353d-94a4-48f1ba519128",
                        "source_sense_id": "d9231596-91e6-3541-b138-7beef7a991bf",
                        "source_sense_description": "LKW mit mindestens einem Anhänger",
                        "target_lang_word": "juggernaut",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "juggernaut",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e1ee438c-b283-3c03-9d98-22f1ea8a9726",
                                        "entry_id": "176cc4a5-7db9-3c9b-9c4b-32ca9fff7dd7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A literal or metaphorical force or object regarded as unstoppable, that will crush all in its path."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8009a30e-65d5-4b32-ba31-1809de556786",
                                                "sense_id": "e1ee438c-b283-3c03-9d98-22f1ea8a9726",
                                                "text": "[…] poor Johnny Tetterby staggering under his Moloch of an infant, the Juggernaut that crushes all his enjoyments."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15527b3b-dd4c-4266-962a-fdf47aebc3e6",
                                                "sense_id": "e1ee438c-b283-3c03-9d98-22f1ea8a9726",
                                                "text": "McCarthy will point to their bad luck but the statistics now show that Wolves have lost four league matches and have claimed one point from a possible 15 - so it may prove to be another difficult season for the Midlands side.\nIn contrast, the Newcastle juggernaut rolls on."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e1597ce-ed96-41a3-90cd-12688d6bf188",
                                                "sense_id": "e1ee438c-b283-3c03-9d98-22f1ea8a9726",
                                                "text": "The fact that the juggernaut of Indian English rolls inexorably on, largely unconcerned by the academic arguments taking place about it, is in itself an indicator of an endonormative force in the variety, and this can be traced historically."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "984ac76d-4407-493b-b035-d76dbf80acec",
                                                "sense_id": "e1ee438c-b283-3c03-9d98-22f1ea8a9726",
                                                "text": "It’s always fun when something massive comes along and sweeps the board, giving everything else a thoroughly good kicking – think Titanic, The Silence of the Lambs, or Lord of the Rings. There’s a sort of deranged, gluttonous feeling, a perverse glee in seeing so many dreams trampled on by a massive cultural juggernaut."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74fa2f0b-4344-363f-b813-8d9c8bc6e4f8",
                                        "entry_id": "176cc4a5-7db9-3c9b-9c4b-32ca9fff7dd7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large, cumbersome truck or lorry, especially an artic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "328d7f03-1a6e-49a0-8e12-07448e0bdba8",
                                                "sense_id": "74fa2f0b-4344-363f-b813-8d9c8bc6e4f8",
                                                "text": "I know I swing me Volvo all around you market square. I know you think that lorry drivers, we just don't care. But the streets are so narrow, built so many years ago. They were built for horses' carts, not juggernauts you know."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fdf9e2d-c8cf-320a-ac23-a86027813d76",
                                        "entry_id": "176cc4a5-7db9-3c9b-9c4b-32ca9fff7dd7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An institution that incites destructive devotion or to which people are carelessly sacrificed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6021308e-d10f-40ee-94c8-7fdf407425a6",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f02d9f4-9d49-353d-94a4-48f1ba519128",
